V. 1. After these things Jesus walked in Galilee-That is, continued there, for some months after the second passover. 

  For he would not walk-Continue in Judea; 

  because the Jews-Those of them who did not believe; and in particular the chief priests, scribes, and Pharisees, sought an opportunity to kill him.

V. 4. For no man doth any thing-Of this kind, in secret; 

  but rather desireth to be of public use. 

  If thou really dost these things-These miracles which are reported; 

  show thyself to the world-To all men.
